    "OU"       => "GEN5 OU BALANCE (vanilla control). Scarf Tyranitar (Sand Stream) revenge + Pursuit-trap; Ferrothorn hazards (SR/Spikes/Leech Seed); Gliscor (Poison Heal) EQ/Toxic/Roost stall; Life Orb Latios (Draco/Psyshock) breaker; Choice Band Scizor Bullet Punch/U-turn/Pursuit; Serene Grace Jirachi (Iron Head flinch + Wish). Set hazards, pivot, wear down, revenge with Scarf/priority.",
    "OUBalance"=> "OU BALANCE (fusion). Ferrothorn/Skarmory sets hazards (SR/Spikes) + Whirlwind phazes setup; Gliscor/Suicune (Poison Heal, EQ/Toxic/Roost) walls + pivots; Rotom/Gyarados (Levitate) VoltTurns + Will-O-Wisp burns; Starmie/Tentacruel Rapid-Spins hazards away (only hazard control). TWO win-cons: (1) Dragonite/Scizor (Multiscale Dragon Dance, Ice-neutral) DD-sweeps late; (2) Marowak/Mimikyu = your BREAKER - USE IT ACTIVELY. Its Disguise BLOCKS THE FIRST HIT, so switch it in freely on a resisted/weak attack and Swords Dance for FREE; Thick Club DOUBLES its Attack so Bonemerang (Ground) and Play Rough (Fairy) hit ENORMOUSLY (dual STAB); Shadow Sneak is PRIORITY to revenge-kill weakened or faster threats. Plan: bring Marowak/Mimikyu in behind Disguise, Swords Dance once, then sweep or Shadow-Sneak-snipe. Wear them down with hazards + walls, then close with a boosted Dragozor OR a Thick-Club Marowak.",
    "OURain"   => "OU RAIN (fusion) - this is a MOMENTUM/WEATHER team, not a spam-your-best-move team. Politoed/Whimsicott sets Drizzle on entry. KEY MECHANIC: weather abilities fire slowest-LAST, so leading Politoed WINS the weather war even against a faster opposing sand/sun setter (your Drizzle overwrites theirs) - do NOT fear leading it into their weather setter. THE WIN CONDITION: after rain is up, IMMEDIATELY U-TURN into a Swift Swim sweeper - Kingdra/Empoleon (special breaker, Draco/Hydro Pump) or Ludicolo/Sceptile (special, resists Water/Electric). In rain Swift Swimmers DOUBLE Speed (~470-670) and outrun the entire field - that is how you sweep. U-turn keeps momentum even when you move second. Azumarill/Marowak (Huge Power + Thick Club = QUADRUPLED Atk, Water/Ground ELECTRIC-IMMUNE) = PRIORITY NUKE that LOVES rain: AQUA JET is priority Water STAB, boosted by rain x1.5 on TOP of x4 Atk - it revenge-kills/cleans almost anything regardless of speed; Earthquake/Knock Off coverage, Swords Dance to end games. It is SLOW, lean on Aqua Jet priority (note: pure-Water foes RESIST it - use EQ/Knock Off there). Only STAY IN with Politoed to Scald/Ice Beam/Encore when there is a clear reason (revenge a low-HP foe, Encore-lock a setup sweeper, or no safe pivot) - do NOT just click Scald every turn. If your rain gets overwritten, bring Politoed back in to RE-SET it (it wins on entry). Swift Swimmers are frail Life Orb glass - pivot with U-turn, don't sit and get worn. Ferrothorn/Skarmory sets hazards + is the backbone. Dragonite/Scizor = rain-INDEPENDENT Dragon Dance wincon for when rain is contested.",
