    "OUSand"   => "OU SAND (fusion). Tyranitar/Articuno (BULKY Rock/Flying anchor, Sand Stream) sets Stealth Rock + STONE EDGE (OHKOs Fire/Fairy sun setters, 4x) + U-TURN pivot + ROOST for longevity. Sand is PERMANENT in IF, so you don't need the setter alive to KEEP sand - but KEEP TYRANITAR/ARTICUNO ALIVE to RE-SET sand if a foe overwrites your weather (rain/sun/hail = weather war); its bulk + Roost let it TANK weather-boosted hits, re-set sand by switching back in, and keep laying hazards - use that, don't trade it cheaply. WEATHER-WAR MECHANIC: weather abilities fire slowest-LAST, so to reclaim weather SWITCH Tyranitar/Articuno back IN after the foe's weather is up (its Sand Stream fires on entry, overwrites). It is Rock/Flying = 2x weak to Water: vs rain-boosted Scald/Hydro Pump, Roost or pivot rather than sitting to die. Sand Rush Slaking/Sandslash is DEAD WEIGHT without sand (just base speed), so winning the weather war IS the game vs other weather teams - keep the setter and re-flip the weather rather than forcing sweeps under enemy weather. Metagross/Garchomp = Choice Scarf revenge killer (Steel/Ground RESISTS Ice, EQ/Iron Head/Outrage/Stone Edge). Ferrothorn/Skarmory hazards (SR/Spikes/Leech) + Whirlwind phaze. Slaking/Sandslash = SAND RUSH sweeper (DOUBLES Speed in sand, ~552): Swords Dance then sweep with THOUSAND ARROWS (Ground move that HITS Flying/Levitate + Steel/Flying - no immunities) + Ice Punch; also RAPID SPINS your hazards away. Regirock/Gliscor (POISON HEAL + Toxic Orb = heals 12.5%/turn once poisoned, BURN/status-immune after orb activates) = utility tank: Def 436 walls physical threats (Sucker Punch/CC/EQ users), and as a ROCK type its SpD is x1.5 IN SAND (~330 effective) so it takes special hits too; Rock/FLYING = IMMUNE to Earthquake/Ground and immune to Spikes. KNOCK OFF strips items, TOXIC clocks non-Steel/Poison walls, PROTECT banks free Poison Heal + toxic ticks - the classic loop: Toxic the target, Protect, Knock Off. Dragonite/Scizor (Multiscale) Dragon Dance wincon. Grind with sand+hazards, revenge with Scarf, Spin off hazards, sweep late with SD Sandslash or DD Dragozor.",
    "Ubers1"   => "UBERS BALANCE (fusion). Darkrai/Hydreigon (Levitate) Nasty Plot + Dark Pulse/Draco special breaker; Kyogre/Mew (Drizzle) Spore + Water Spout + Quiver Dance; Groudon/Gliscor (Poison Heal, Toxic Orb) Swords Dance EQ wall+sweeper, immune Ground+Electric; Kyurem/Metagross (Choice Scarf, Clear Body) revenge - Iron Head is your Fairy/Xerneas answer, Icicle Crash 4x's Gliscor/Dragons; Slaking/Dragonite (Multiscale, NO Truant) Extreme Speed priority wincon; Dialga/Espeon (Magic Bounce) bounces hazards/status + Stealth Rock + Calm Mind. Wall, phaze/scarf-revenge, then sweep with the Multiscale priority mon.",
    "Ubers2"   => "UBERS RAIN OFFENSE (fusion). Kyogre/Celebi (Drizzle) Specs Water Spout nuke; Kingdra/Zekrom (Swift Swim) Dragon Dance + Bolt Strike/Waterfall (doubled speed in rain); Palkia/Flygon (Levitate, Ground-immune) Calm Mind special breaker. Groudon/Gliscor (Poison Heal SD) + Aegislash/Lugia (Multiscale, Spectral Thief STEALS boosts + Whirlwind phaze) + Registeel/Ferrothorn (Steel/Grass, resists Electric, hazards + Power Whip) are the spine so you aren't pure glass. Overwhelm in rain, fall back on the spine, phaze setup.",
